# Git — implement first, PR only on request

The user owns `main`. Never land work there. Never merge PRs.

## Default

Implement. Leave **uncommitted**. No `commit` / `push` / `gh pr create` until
asked. “PR” means open one, not merge.

## Commit

Conventional Commits (English) **and push immediately**. No PR unless asked.
If a PR is already open, edit title/body for **every** commit on the branch.
No test suites on commit unless this is the user’s test pass.

## PR

1. Branch off `main` (`feat/…` / `fix/…`). Not on `main`. One concern per PR.
2. Missing behavior tests → `testing.mdc`, run once. Then commit, push, open
   a PR whose body covers all commits.
3. Checks: `quality`, `api-test`, `web-e2e`. Diagnose failures per
   `agent-efficiency.mdc`. Do not watch green CI.
4. Stop. Give the PR URL.

Later commits: push and refresh the PR body.

## `main` updates

`update-open-prs.yml` updates same-repo PR heads. Fallback: fetch, **merge**
`origin/main` into the PR head, push (no rebase, no force). Skip the branch
that just merged. Conflicts: stop that PR, continue others. Do not fast-forward
local `main` unless asked.

## Never

Unprompted commit/push/PR (except merging `origin/main` into open PR heads).
No push to `main`. No `gh pr merge`. No force-push to `main`.

## After they merge

Do not recreate the deleted head. Sync remaining PRs. `git fetch --prune` and
delete the local branch if it remains. After pull/switch: `npm run build:packages`.
